Ed301/X301 test vector provenance
================================

Repository: https://github.com/ychromosome/ed301
Source commit: 9ef3fc21e0f79331f1c885907cf2805f5d2698aa
The JSON files are byte-for-byte copies of vectors/ at that commit.

SHA-256:
4dbbd93f5814f4e676b8007b13973037a7924872d46d328cdaeb314cd3190e82  ed301-eddsa-v2.json
b675f677f0d717a09f3c1cc55bf0c2ad97d17ca14a7890565a41916222cc80f0  x301-v2.json

The tests use the existing load_text_file()/get_json_string() helpers,
with array/object, boolean, integer and hex helpers for this corpus.
Fixed-size crypto_api.h calls cannot express variable key/signature lengths;
those vectors exercise the same provider's EVP import/verification boundary
with their actual lengths. No vector is padded or truncated.

point_decoding.accepted describes point decoding, not public-key policy.
Identity and torsion points decode but are invalid Ed301 public keys. These
entries are checked against the stricter public-key import policy; the base
point imports successfully. Field/scalar codec internals are not a separate
SSH primitive and are not reimplemented. X301 evaluations and all iteration
checkpoints are covered in addition to the required key/DH/error categories.
